WEBVTT

00:01.950 --> 00:03.830
At the dawn of the Seika era,

00:03.830 --> 00:06.610
in order to regulate unwanted messages that presented a bad influence to society,

00:06.610 --> 00:08.950
the Media Cleansing Act was passed.

00:08.950 --> 00:12.410
The libraries armed themselves in order to protect freedom of expression

00:12.410 --> 00:15.200
from the extreme censorship of the Media Cleansing Committee.

00:15.200 --> 00:18.600
The conflict between the two continued to escalate.

00:18.600 --> 00:24.360
In the 31st year of Seika, a stupid girl plunged herself into the middle of that conflict without letting her parents know.

00:24.360 --> 00:26.640
"Stupid," Sir?

00:33.030 --> 00:37.630
usu murasaki hirogaru

00:33.030 --> 00:37.630
The faint purple spreads across the sky

00:37.630 --> 00:45.610
orenji iro ni kawaru mado no soto

00:37.630 --> 00:45.610
The color changes to orange outside the window

00:45.610 --> 00:49.660
yoru wa mou bai bai

00:45.610 --> 00:49.660
The night's already "bye-bye"

00:50.210 --> 00:55.900
tada kirei na mono wo kirei to

00:50.210 --> 00:55.900
I just want to be someone who

00:55.900 --> 01:00.460
ieru atashi de itai

00:55.900 --> 01:00.460
calls beautiful things beautiful

01:00.460 --> 01:06.800
ima wa dokidoki shitai no

01:00.460 --> 01:06.800
I want to get excited for it!

01:07.330 --> 01:11.860
fumidashichae tomaranai

01:07.330 --> 01:11.860
So I step out, unstoppable

01:11.860 --> 01:16.450
zenbu te ni hairi sou de

01:11.860 --> 01:16.450
And take everything into my own hands

01:16.940 --> 01:21.050
sono saki de aitai

01:16.940 --> 01:21.050
Beyond there, I want to meet

01:21.050 --> 01:27.040
mita koto no nai atashi

01:21.050 --> 01:27.040
the new self that I've never seen

01:27.510 --> 01:32.160
sayonara daisuki na machi

01:27.510 --> 01:32.160
Farewell, my beloved town

01:32.160 --> 01:36.710
atashi mo ganbatte miru yo

01:32.160 --> 01:36.710
I'll try to do my best

01:36.710 --> 01:44.270
kono sora no tsuzuku basho de

01:36.710 --> 01:44.270
somewhere under the same sky

01:49.560 --> 01:56.420
Kasahara Iku, 22 years old, is the first female ever to be a member of the Kanto Library Force's Task Force.

01:57.690 --> 02:03.350
However, an emergency situation has arisen; her conservative parents are coming to see her workplace.

02:04.560 --> 02:10.450
There is even the possibility of forced deportation if they discover her actual position.

02:12.930 --> 02:15.110
This is her biggest crisis since she joined the Force.

02:15.110 --> 02:18.670
Will she be able to survive it?

02:20.910 --> 02:25.360
Situation 05

02:20.910 --> 02:25.360
Operation
Disturb-the-Parents

02:25.380 --> 02:29.350
Special Cover Story

02:25.380 --> 02:29.350
Full Report on the Battle of the Musuem of History

02:25.380 --> 02:29.350
Performance of the Kanto Library Force

02:26.480 --> 02:28.880
It was a pretty good article.

02:30.120 --> 02:32.860
You can read it if you want.

02:38.710 --> 02:40.680
They used quite a few pages.

02:40.680 --> 02:43.370
This must be quite a blow to the Cleansing Committee, too.

02:43.370 --> 02:45.120
Kasahara, don't you want to read it as well?

02:45.120 --> 02:47.380
I'll be taken back home if they find out.

02:47.380 --> 02:49.770
No, I must persevere.

02:49.770 --> 02:52.620
Good luck, me!

02:53.230 --> 02:55.790
Oh yeah, I guess it's today.

02:55.790 --> 02:58.260
The biggest stunt of your life, right?

02:58.260 --> 03:01.220
Do you think she can act as a library administrator?

03:01.220 --> 03:06.350
Dear God, dear Buddha, dear Prince, please protect me through the—

03:06.620 --> 03:08.380
Excuse me.

03:08.380 --> 03:10.220
Your parents are here.

03:13.860 --> 03:15.840
Give up already.

03:15.840 --> 03:20.210
It's all your fault for not telling your parents.

03:20.210 --> 03:22.610
Go already.

03:24.810 --> 03:26.320
Hey, Kasahara,

03:26.880 --> 03:29.490
wouldn't this be bad?

03:33.060 --> 03:35.370
Oh my god!

03:36.710 --> 03:41.590
I-I'm glad to see you... doing well...

03:41.590 --> 03:43.540
What's with that?

03:43.620 --> 03:46.020
She stuttered in front of her parents?

03:47.290 --> 03:50.170
Where have you been anyway?

03:50.560 --> 03:52.500
Aren't you working in the library?

03:52.500 --> 03:55.620
I-I was in the underground vault.

03:55.620 --> 03:58.320
I'll be on this floor tomorrow, so everything's fine.

03:58.320 --> 04:01.220
How will I be fine?!

04:01.220 --> 04:05.060
Iku, please tell me there'll be no censorship today.

04:05.060 --> 04:07.390
If there's a raid...

04:07.390 --> 04:10.320
I-It's not like they happen every day!

04:10.320 --> 04:12.120
This is painful to watch.

04:12.120 --> 04:14.190
She must be so scared.

04:14.190 --> 04:17.940
She sweat so much last night that she had to change her pajamas at one point.

04:17.940 --> 04:19.670
In this season?

04:20.250 --> 04:22.150
Shall we have a look around?

04:22.150 --> 04:24.850
We looked around the whole place while we were waiting.

04:24.850 --> 04:28.380
Iku, we want to see the inside of the base as well.

04:30.920 --> 04:37.380
Instructor Dojo, would you explain to them that the base is off-limits to non-staffers?

04:37.380 --> 04:39.090
Idiot!

04:39.090 --> 04:42.140
I can't lie to them when there's a designated tour route!

04:43.900 --> 04:47.010
Then, Shibasaki, please come with us.

04:47.010 --> 04:49.920
No way. I don't want to do PR jobs like that.

04:49.920 --> 04:52.390
Then would you...

04:52.390 --> 04:54.300
I'm your superior officer!

04:54.300 --> 04:57.500
What if they ask me about your performance?

04:57.500 --> 05:03.350
"She's terrible at learning library duties, clumsy, careless, and hopeless."

05:03.350 --> 05:05.100
I'd have no choice but to tell them the truth.

05:05.100 --> 05:07.310
Hey! I'm not—

05:07.310 --> 05:09.630
Tone it down, you two.

05:13.110 --> 05:16.260
Shibasaki, go with them.

05:17.840 --> 05:22.040
I'll buy you something later, so please help me, damnit!

05:22.040 --> 05:24.230
Lunch out, dessert included.

05:24.250 --> 05:26.730
Deal!

05:33.970 --> 05:36.300
It looks kind of scary.

05:36.300 --> 05:39.400
It's better than getting yelled at by instructors.

05:40.410 --> 05:42.570
Right, Kasahara-san?

05:42.950 --> 05:44.300
Yeah.

05:44.300 --> 05:45.530
Was that on purpose?!

05:45.530 --> 05:48.620
What is this helicopter used for?

05:48.620 --> 05:52.700
Transporting goods and injured people, and also for training.

05:52.700 --> 05:55.950
It can actually carry 15 people.

05:57.000 --> 05:59.030
This is the cafeteria.

05:59.030 --> 06:02.180
It looks rather aged.

06:04.060 --> 06:07.670
LSTC Genda, these are LFC Kasahara's parents.

06:07.670 --> 06:09.640
Hello, I'm Genda.

06:09.640 --> 06:13.530
He's the superior officer who's been taking care of us ever since we arrived here.

06:13.870 --> 06:15.980
Thank you for looking after her.

06:15.980 --> 06:19.540
She performed quite the heroic act the other day.

06:19.540 --> 06:21.250
Heroic?

06:21.250 --> 06:23.120
You haven't heard?

06:23.120 --> 06:24.010
A couple of weeks ago...

06:24.010 --> 06:25.410
LSTC Genda!

06:25.700 --> 06:29.210
We need you right now. Please come with me.

06:29.560 --> 06:31.130
Wait a minute.

06:31.130 --> 06:34.590
Do you have any lodging arrangements?

06:34.820 --> 06:39.590
We have plenty of lodging space, so do stay here.

06:41.190 --> 06:43.950
Shall we take him up on his offer?

06:43.950 --> 06:48.210
Dojo, you take care of showing him to the men's dorm.

06:52.510 --> 06:57.310
Did I hear my daughter call you Instructor?

06:57.310 --> 06:58.720
Kasaha—

06:59.170 --> 07:04.150
I was LFC Kasahara's instructor during her training.

07:04.150 --> 07:06.580
She probably can't get over the old habit.

07:06.960 --> 07:11.040
It seems she trusts you a great deal.

07:12.470 --> 07:16.050
Sorry, d-do you really think so?

07:16.050 --> 07:21.260
She came to you first when seeking help at the Library.

07:23.460 --> 07:25.600
What's the room like?

07:25.600 --> 07:26.920
Let me see it.

07:26.920 --> 07:30.480
No! It's not just my room!

07:30.640 --> 07:32.510
Go ahead.

07:32.510 --> 07:35.430
Shibasaki!

07:38.440 --> 07:39.810
Excuse me.

07:39.810 --> 07:41.130
Oh...

07:41.130 --> 07:42.870
Hey!

07:49.680 --> 07:52.260
What can I see from here?

07:55.180 --> 07:56.560
Could this be...

07:56.560 --> 07:59.010
That's mine.

08:03.770 --> 08:05.420
I appreciate your effort.

08:05.420 --> 08:06.970
I really do, but...

08:07.140 --> 08:10.430
it clearly doesn't fit you!

08:13.250 --> 08:16.520
It belongs to my boyfriend. He works in the Defense Force.

08:18.080 --> 08:19.650
It's a secret, okay?

08:21.590 --> 08:23.360
Good job, Shibasaki!

08:23.800 --> 08:29.330
Shibasaki-san is dainty, graceful, and very caring.

08:29.830 --> 08:33.450
She's what all ladies should be like.

08:33.450 --> 08:35.020
Right.

08:35.020 --> 08:39.450
And I'm big and hot-headed...

08:41.870 --> 08:43.430
What happened here?

08:44.390 --> 08:46.140
It's nothing.

08:46.660 --> 08:49.850
Well, I'm done.

09:04.770 --> 09:09.410
Does she want me to be like Shibasaki?

09:28.370 --> 09:30.100
Good night.

09:37.430 --> 09:39.630
It's for your own good.

09:39.630 --> 09:42.140
I'm very worried.

09:42.140 --> 09:44.100
Don't decide for me!

09:44.100 --> 09:48.370
Iku, why won't you try to understand how your mother feels?

10:10.300 --> 10:12.010
I feel your pain.

10:12.010 --> 10:14.650
I heard your parents stayed in the dorm.

10:14.650 --> 10:16.550
Shush!

10:18.670 --> 10:23.040
Even though you had your assignment changed, you still might ruin it!

10:23.040 --> 10:25.290
Are you okay?

10:25.290 --> 10:27.940
It was just a careless mistake!

10:27.940 --> 10:30.730
What part of you isn't careless?

10:30.730 --> 10:34.040
Shut up, you mini-Dojo!

10:36.610 --> 10:39.270
Hey, look.

10:46.930 --> 10:49.200
Should I handle those?

10:49.200 --> 10:50.620
Thank you!

10:50.620 --> 10:53.580
May I help you?

10:53.580 --> 10:56.730
Oh, Iku.

10:57.920 --> 11:00.320
What?!

11:03.680 --> 11:04.770
What now?!

11:04.770 --> 11:05.900
You have got to be kidding me!

11:06.770 --> 11:09.820
Oh boy, they're all out of order!

11:09.820 --> 11:10.810
What a pain!

11:10.810 --> 11:16.270
Would you hand me the issue with "Kanto Library Force" on the cover?

11:16.810 --> 11:19.850
Looks like someone has it checked out.

11:19.850 --> 11:21.540
Step aside!

11:24.030 --> 11:25.540
What was this incident?

11:25.540 --> 11:27.640
That's...

11:28.150 --> 11:32.830
It's the one where they fought in Odawara, right?

11:33.150 --> 11:35.070
A couple of weeks ago, right?

11:35.070 --> 11:36.560
Y-Yes.

11:36.740 --> 11:41.470
I think you'll get a better idea if you start with the previous issues.

11:42.920 --> 11:43.980
Like this one.

11:43.980 --> 11:45.290
Really.

11:45.290 --> 11:48.200
I'll go read this, then.

11:54.990 --> 11:57.350
Volatile material should be isolated immediately!

11:57.350 --> 12:00.300
Idiot, don't bring it here!

12:00.300 --> 12:04.260
Besides, the newest issue cannot be checked out for two weeks.

12:04.260 --> 12:06.840
But if I leave it out there, my parents will...

12:06.840 --> 12:09.510
Can't we make an exception?

12:09.510 --> 12:11.040
No.

12:11.280 --> 12:12.590
But...

12:12.590 --> 12:14.210
The Second Declaration!

12:14.480 --> 12:17.770
The Second Declaration of the Library's Freedom.

12:18.280 --> 12:21.740
The Library has the freedom to provide information.

12:23.100 --> 12:28.790
Don't take away the freedom of access from the users, no matter what circumstance you're in.

12:28.790 --> 12:30.120
Yes, Sir.

12:30.120 --> 12:33.830
There's a constant stream of readers for the newest issue.

12:33.830 --> 12:38.240
Why don't you divert your parents' attention when that issue gets returned to the shelf?

12:38.240 --> 12:39.610
Right!

12:39.610 --> 12:41.210
I'll try that!

13:02.840 --> 13:05.150
This is the issue after that one!

13:05.410 --> 13:06.960
Thanks.

13:19.320 --> 13:22.270
Didn't you like this person?

13:22.790 --> 13:26.010
This issue was sold out everywhere!

13:26.010 --> 13:27.790
Great!

13:27.790 --> 13:29.370
Thank you!

13:31.280 --> 13:32.880
Excuse me.

13:32.880 --> 13:34.010
Yes?

13:34.010 --> 13:38.490
I would like to read the general summary of this year's affairs.

13:38.490 --> 13:40.100
Do you have anything like that?

13:40.400 --> 13:42.980
What's he trying to do?

13:43.180 --> 13:48.570
So, you want the headline news for the year, right?

13:55.940 --> 13:58.350
All right, piece of cake.

13:58.880 --> 14:01.860
Here are the books you requested.

14:08.400 --> 14:09.870
These are last year's.

14:09.870 --> 14:11.270
No way!

14:13.850 --> 14:17.680
Right, this year's news is published under next year's title!

14:18.060 --> 14:21.400
Sorry, I'll bring them right away!

14:27.230 --> 14:28.530
Not here?

14:28.870 --> 14:30.840
Are they all checked out?

14:31.050 --> 14:32.590
That can't be.

14:32.590 --> 14:34.970
Did we not buy them this year?

14:34.970 --> 14:36.750
That can't be.

14:36.750 --> 14:37.930
Why?

14:37.930 --> 14:39.560
I don't understand.

14:40.370 --> 14:42.460
Instructor Dojo?

14:45.700 --> 14:46.610
I'll go.

14:46.610 --> 14:49.070
But I need to do it.

14:49.070 --> 14:50.970
You idiot.

14:52.080 --> 14:54.650
I don't care about your circumstances.

14:54.650 --> 14:58.710
Our job is to fulfill the users' needs in the shortest amount of time.

14:58.710 --> 15:01.850
Any further mistakes can lead to the loss of the Library's credibility.

15:06.540 --> 15:11.640
The publications on current affairs are used heavily between now and the end of the year,

15:11.640 --> 15:14.240
so we have a special section for them.

15:16.750 --> 15:20.400
It looks like the ones on general affairs are all checked out.

15:20.400 --> 15:23.540
Do you have anything else you recommend?

15:23.540 --> 15:26.170
What kind of publication would you like?

15:26.350 --> 15:30.300
Works that are easy to read, and those that contain historical backgrounds.

15:31.610 --> 15:33.230
Well...

15:35.550 --> 15:37.600
How about these?

15:42.000 --> 15:44.150
Thank you.

15:47.350 --> 15:49.480
That was perfect.

15:50.640 --> 15:53.190
He gave me the answer right away.

15:56.830 --> 15:58.730
You asked Tezuka too?

15:58.730 --> 16:02.960
Comparing you with a co-worker from the same year is the best way to find out how well you're doing.

16:02.960 --> 16:05.700
Aren't you doing a disappointing job?

16:05.700 --> 16:07.200
This sucks.

16:07.200 --> 16:09.460
He really was testing me.

16:09.640 --> 16:12.120
Tezuka is especially good, though!

16:12.120 --> 16:14.380
Don't compare me with such a monster!

16:14.510 --> 16:16.840
Then, can I compare you with Shibasaki-san?

16:16.840 --> 16:18.890
She's special too!

16:19.220 --> 16:24.520
If everyone else is so good, how could you become a librarian?

16:26.610 --> 16:28.240
Thief!

16:32.950 --> 16:33.630
Wait!

16:33.630 --> 16:34.360
Let me go!

16:43.430 --> 16:46.460
Don't underestimate my legs!

16:55.960 --> 16:57.370
Good job!

16:57.370 --> 16:59.010
Hey...

17:09.580 --> 17:11.690
Now I've done it.

17:11.800 --> 17:15.200
Maybe there'll be a family inquisition.

17:21.410 --> 17:28.990
Well, since she can run so fast, she helps with security cases like today's.

17:28.990 --> 17:33.210
What do you think of her as a member of the library's staff?

17:40.160 --> 17:41.760
She's still lacking.

17:43.870 --> 17:49.400
But her passion to protect books is truly pure.

17:49.400 --> 17:52.380
Then, how is she as your subordinate?

17:52.380 --> 17:53.850
Very valuable!

17:54.390 --> 17:58.990
She's lacking right now, but I believe she will be a good librarian.

18:00.310 --> 18:02.410
I'm glad it's you.

18:04.570 --> 18:06.460
Honor the Media Cleansing Act!

18:06.460 --> 18:07.910
Disband immediately!

18:07.910 --> 18:08.510
The Library Force...

18:08.510 --> 18:12.060
Won't they get violent?

18:14.510 --> 18:17.600
Sometimes violent groups do come,

18:17.600 --> 18:21.290
but Security seizes them and hands them over to the police.

18:21.290 --> 18:23.810
I don't care what the procedure is.

18:23.810 --> 18:25.990
They use guns too, don't they?

18:25.990 --> 18:29.130
What if you get hit by a stray shot?

18:29.980 --> 18:36.110
Iku, can you ask for a day off when a censorship seems imminent?

18:36.760 --> 18:38.950
Everyone's in the same situation, though!

18:38.950 --> 18:40.350
It's our job!

18:40.350 --> 18:44.320
Shibasaki also does what her boss tells her to do during a censorship!

18:45.770 --> 18:49.740
I was very worried that you might have gotten hurt yesterday.

18:49.740 --> 18:52.660
You shouldn't be working here.

18:52.660 --> 18:55.620
You don't care if it's someone else then?

18:55.620 --> 18:57.870
I do, but...

18:58.170 --> 19:00.340
Would you leave the library, and come work—

19:00.340 --> 19:02.580
If that's what you want, I'm going.

19:02.580 --> 19:04.710
Sit down for a bit.

19:13.400 --> 19:16.400
Don't ask her to quit so easily.

19:19.730 --> 19:23.860
This is the work Iku pondered and chose on her own.

19:24.550 --> 19:26.240
But...

19:26.490 --> 19:29.110
Let's accept her decision.

19:30.150 --> 19:31.710
Dad...

19:31.710 --> 19:33.960
You're siding with me...

19:34.550 --> 19:38.920
Why did you want to become a librarian?

19:41.090 --> 19:42.880
That's...

19:53.010 --> 19:56.770
Oh my, that sounds like a prince!

19:58.800 --> 20:04.240
Anyway, I just wished that I could protect books like he did.

20:04.500 --> 20:08.290
That's the first time you've told us, but it's a wonderful reason, isn't it?

20:14.050 --> 20:15.910
Please take care of yourselves.

20:15.910 --> 20:18.420
And you, too.

20:27.610 --> 20:28.880
I'm sorry...

20:29.260 --> 20:31.290
I didn't tell you the truth.

20:37.060 --> 20:39.770
Please look after Iku.

20:44.890 --> 20:46.190
Yes, Sir.

21:01.690 --> 21:03.490
Oh, man.

21:06.690 --> 21:10.030
nani ka ga kawaru kigashita

21:06.690 --> 21:10.030
I had a feeling something was about to change

21:10.030 --> 21:13.410
nani mo kawaranu asa ni

21:10.030 --> 21:13.410
on this very ordinary morning

21:13.410 --> 21:18.420
itsu mo yori sukoshi ii mezamedatta

21:13.410 --> 21:18.420
I woke up feeling a little better than usual

21:20.080 --> 21:26.760
hito sashiyubi de sashimesu no wa mirai

21:20.080 --> 21:26.760
My index finger points out to the future

21:26.760 --> 21:36.430
kimi no te no hira ga fureru tabi ni afuru omoi

21:26.760 --> 21:36.430
My thoughts overflow each time I touch your palm

21:36.880 --> 21:40.410
ch-ch-ch-changes saa kawatteku

21:36.880 --> 21:40.410
Changes, yeah. I'm changing.

21:40.410 --> 21:43.730
sayonara furui jibun

21:40.410 --> 21:43.730
Goodbye my old self

21:43.730 --> 21:50.260
shingenjitsu atarashii nani ka ga matteru

21:43.730 --> 21:50.260
There's something new awaiting me in the new reality

21:50.260 --> 21:54.000
ch-ch-ch-changes saa kawatteku

21:50.260 --> 21:54.000
Changes, yeah. I'm changing.

21:54.000 --> 21:57.230
ushinau mono mo aru

21:54.000 --> 21:57.230
There are things I'll lose too

21:57.230 --> 22:03.000
demo iindesu hitotsu unazuki kakedasu

21:57.230 --> 22:03.000
But that's okay, I'll just nod and keep running

22:03.000 --> 22:10.550
saa subete ga ima kawatteku subete ga hajimaru

22:03.000 --> 22:10.550
Yeah, everything is changing now, everything starts now

22:10.550 --> 22:20.840
shingenjitsu dare no mono demo nai atarashii jibun

22:10.550 --> 22:20.840
It's a new reality, my new self belongs to no one but me
